# No apps outside Cursor

**Do not launch, install, control, or automate any application outside Cursor.**

**NO EXCEPTIONS.** Not if the user asks. Not for screenshots. Not for debugging. Not for “just checking.” Not headless. Not ever.

Forbidden examples (not a complete list):

- Chrome, Chromium, Safari, Firefox, Edge, Brave
- Playwright, Puppeteer, Selenium, or any browser automation
- `npx playwright`, `playwright install`, or installing browser binaries
- `open` (macOS) to start a GUI app
- Any command whose purpose is to run an app outside Cursor

For UI questions: ask the user, or read code/HTML/CSS/build output in the workspace. Nothing else.
